Spec out a more principled, ecosystem-aware design for BLOCKERS.md resolution/urgency. Current glance column is just a raw count of unresolved bullets per project -- it conflates 'needs your decision right now' with 'FYI, waiting on something external' (e.g. crt's DAC-arriving-Tuesday note) and 'in progress, no action needed' (e.g. mid-print status). Worth a real taxonomy (blocking/waiting/fyi or similar), maybe a required tag/field per bullet, and glance logic that only surfaces the genuinely actionable ones by default. Consider whether this should live in BLOCKERS.md's own convention doc or a new docs/ file, and how it interacts with the existing %%TAG/collect-feedback.sh answer-processing flow.
